cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Introduction to Unix
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Steven
    family-names: Morgan
    affiliation: Melbourne Bioinformatics, University of Melbourne
abstract: >-
  A hands-on introduction to the Unix command line for
  bioinformatics. Designed for participants with little or no
  command-line experience, it covers connecting to a Unix
  machine, navigating and organising the file system, viewing
  and manipulating files, file permissions, searching with
  grep, pipes and redirection, and transferring files between
  local and remote machines.
